    {
        "age": null,
        "album": "",
        "author": "Polygon Staff",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "comments": [],
        "date_created": "2026-08-13T09:26:29.441713+00:00",
        "date_dead_since": null,
        "date_published": "2026-08-13T09:18:47+00:00",
        "description": "How much storytelling can you do with a few yards of cloth? If you're FromSoftware, a whole freaking lot! In Elden Ring and FromSoftware's ever-growing catalog of solemn sword adventures, there's an astounding amount of attention paid to cloth. The shape, the texture, the movement. But why? Polygon's resident man of the cloth Patrick is here to break it all down.#eldenring",
        "id": 6168197,
        "language": "en",
        "link": "https://www.polygon.com/video/elden-ring-does-this-better-than-anyone-else",
        "manual_status_code": 0,
        "page_rating": 27,
        "page_rating_contents": 86,
        "page_rating_visits": 0,
        "page_rating_votes": 0,
        "permanent": false,
        "source__id": 258,
        "source_url": "https://www.polygon.com/rss/index.xml",
        "status_code": 0,
        "tags": [],
        "thumbnail": null,
        "title": "Elden Ring does this better than anyone else",
        "vote": 0
    },
    {
        "age": null,
        "album": "",
        "author": "Polygon Staff",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "comments": [],
        "date_created": "2026-08-13T09:26:29.584270+00:00",
        "date_dead_since": null,
        "date_published": "2026-08-13T09:07:46+00:00",
        "description": "If a horse is in a video game, that means someone busted their butt to get it there. Horses are WEIRD \u2014 they're massive animals with weird bendy joints and many, many gaits. It's no wonder why so many games choose to simply treat them as transportation. Even so, some games go the extra mile to make horses unique and meaningful to the gameplay \u2014 and they benefit from it massively. Here's why horses are so difficult to get into games, and what we're missing out on when horses aren't given their due.#breathofthewild #eldenring",
        "id": 6168198,
        "language": "en",
        "link": "https://www.polygon.com/video/why-horses-are-so-hard-for-video-games-to-get-right",
        "manual_status_code": 0,
        "page_rating": 27,
        "page_rating_contents": 86,
        "page_rating_visits": 0,
        "page_rating_votes": 0,
        "permanent": false,
        "source__id": 258,
        "source_url": "https://www.polygon.com/rss/index.xml",
        "status_code": 0,
        "tags": [],
        "thumbnail": null,
        "title": "Why horses are so hard for video games to get right",
        "vote": 0
    },
    {
        "age": null,
        "album": "",
        "author": "Polygon Staff",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "comments": [],
        "date_created": "2026-08-13T09:26:29.741273+00:00",
        "date_dead_since": null,
        "date_published": "2026-08-13T09:00:20+00:00",
        "description": "Elden Ring's dogs are some of the most annoying enemies for me to wrap my head around in a fight. Even hundreds of hours into the game, one tiny mistake in a fight against a dog threatens to send me spiraling into despair and lost runes. I wanted to figure out what it was about FromSoft's dog-type enemies that made them so obnoxious to fight. So I put away my weapons and put up my fists to every dog in the Lands Between \u2014 including the Monstrous Dogs and the Red Wolf of Radagon \u2014 until I figured out why dogs are a pain in my butt.#eldenring #gameplay",
        "id": 6168199,
        "language": "en",
        "link": "https://www.polygon.com/video/i-hate-dogs-in-elden-ring",
        "manual_status_code": 0,
        "page_rating": 27,
        "page_rating_contents": 86,
        "page_rating_visits": 0,
        "page_rating_votes": 0,
        "permanent": false,
        "source__id": 258,
        "source_url": "https://www.polygon.com/rss/index.xml",
        "status_code": 0,
        "tags": [],
        "thumbnail": null,
        "title": "I hate dogs (in Elden Ring)",
        "vote": 0
    },
    {
        "age": null,
        "album": "",
        "author": "Polygon Staff",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "comments": [],
        "date_created": "2026-08-13T09:26:29.959745+00:00",
        "date_dead_since": null,
        "date_published": "2026-08-13T08:55:29+00:00",
        "description": "Skeletons are a classic video game grunt, but what makes them so special? FromSoftware has mastered the bones of skeleton-making, and their expertise is on full display in Elden Ring. Adventurers have been ragging on skeletons since Gary Gygax co-created Dungeons and Dragons, but our relationship with skellies goes back much further, and Elden Ring draws on myths from all over the world to inspire its funniest (and most annoying) enemies.#eldenring #fromsoftware",
        "id": 6168200,
        "language": "en",
        "link": "https://www.polygon.com/video/the-mythic-origins-of-elden-ring-s-spooky-scary-skeletons",
        "manual_status_code": 0,
        "page_rating": 27,
        "page_rating_contents": 86,
        "page_rating_visits": 0,
        "page_rating_votes": 0,
        "permanent": false,
